{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And garments</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other (Exodus 12:35) \"and they asked of the Egyptians vessels of silver and vessels of gold and garments.\" To teach you that all vessels of silver and gold they took, but garments — each one took only two garments: one to wrap the dough in, as written \"their kneading-troughs wrapped in their garments,\" and one for wearing, and it sufficed for them all the days they were in the wilderness, as written \"your garment did not wear out from upon you.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:11.031941120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}